Third-party dependencies
------------------------

The Python packages listed in requirements.txt / requirements-pinned.txt are not
vendored into this repository: they are installed by whoever runs Aura and remain
under their own licenses. The runtime set is:

- python-telegram-bot (LGPL-3.0)   https://python-telegram-bot.org
- google-genai (Apache-2.0)        https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai
- requests (Apache-2.0)            https://requests.readthedocs.io
- cryptography (Apache-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause)  https://cryptography.io
- python-dotenv (BSD-3-Clause)     https://github.com/theskumar/python-dotenv
- pypdf (BSD-3-Clause)             https://pypdf.readthedocs.io
- python-docx (MIT)                https://python-docx.readthedocs.io
- openpyxl (MIT)                   https://openpyxl.readthedocs.io
- python-pptx (MIT)                https://python-pptx.readthedocs.io
- resvg-py (MPL-2.0 wrapper of resvg, MPL-2.0)  https://github.com/baseplate-admin/resvg-py
- tzdata (Apache-2.0)              https://pypi.org/project/tzdata

The test suite adds pytest, ruff, pre-commit and their dependencies; see
requirements-dev.txt. None of them ship with the application.

Sticker pack
------------

`stickers_config.json` names a sticker set that lives on Telegram
(`sYMA1791362612_by_stickwebot`). No sticker image is stored or redistributed
here: Aura keeps Telegram's own file identifiers in `bot.db` after the bot has
been granted access to the set, and operators are expected to point the file at
their own set instead.

External services
-----------------

Aura calls Google Gemini, Telegram Bot API, You.com, Pollinations.ai,
Open-Meteo and meme-api.com. No data, keys, or assets from those services are
redistributed here, and using them is subject to their own terms.
